    "HAND-BUILT manifest entry, not tools/tubuild.py create output -- the `main` module is unsegmentable, so there is no create candidate id.",
    "Message is the tree's existing class name (include/Message.h); the `3` suffix follows the tree's numeric style (d_s_mg_jump2.cpp next to d_s_mg_jump.cpp) per Juan's 2026-10-11 new-file rule -- fold onto the established name, never coin one.",
    "Message is NOT polymorphic -- no RTTI, no vtable, no ctor/dtor -- and every member here is static. The VS text path drives one shared render state around 0x0209fc50 plus the blob pointers at 0x0209fd00..0x0209fd1c.",
    "#pragma defer_codegen off gives source-order emission: src/Message3.cpp lists definitions ROM-ascending and the emitted section order is ROM-ascending. Deferred codegen was unusable because the optimization-pragma functions (func_02031428, func_020326ac and func_02033bb8, all opt_common_subs) would read their offs last-wins at end of file. The opt_strength_reduction brackets on func_020331fc, func_02033e50 and func_02033bb8 were removed once the second tilemap row was indexed as (scr + i)[0x20] (#821).",
    "The address-named helpers and the named C helpers LoadFont3D and Message_DrawCenteredLineVS keep extern \"C\" linkage. AddCharVS is a static member like its single-player twin Message::AddChar. data_0209f4a4 is consumed through decl_common.h's s16[] spelling; func_020326ac reads it through a byte-stride pointer pun, so the (u8*) cast stays at the use site.",
    "_ZN3OAM6RenderEbP7OamAttriiii5Fix12IiES3_ii keeps the literal-name spelling with scalar params (Fix12 wall).",
    "The nine 0x02030fa8..0x020319fc shards were folded in ROM order ahead of AddCharVS. func_02031028's glyph-table search keeps its inline predicate, now `bool`: an int-returning or open-coded compare swaps the two cmp operands.",
    "LOCAL WORKER NOTE: this machine builds the EU-dump control ROM ddab9300b24aeae254192c2a30d812b07ece3adff83230e75c865ed915c9de40, byte-identical to its strict stock control; verification.linkcheck.rom.sha256 is normalized to the fleet-canonical hash per #3691."
